jq
Usage: jq [-r] 'FILTER' FILE

Parses and filters json -- which is what nearly every other tool here emits.
Pull one value out of a wall of output, walk an array, reshape records. The
filter is a little path language: `.key`, `.arr[]`, `.a.b`.

	'.key'        the value at a top-level key
	'.arr[]'      every element of an array, one per line
	-r            raw output: strings without their quotes

See also: rg, python
